   "id": "math.sigma-properties",
   "name": "Properties of sigma notation",
   "requires": [],
   "explain": {
    "en": {
     "text": "Constants come out of a sum: ∑ c·aₖ = c ∑ aₖ. A sum of two rules splits into two sums, and so does a difference. A sum of a constant c over n terms is nc. A long sum can be split into two parts at any point."
    },
    "am": {
     "text": "ቋሚ ቁጥር ከድምሩ ውጭ ይወጣል፤ የሁለት ሕጎች ድምር ወደ ሁለት ድምሮች ይከፈላል። በ n ተርሞች ላይ የቋሚ c ድምር nc ነው።",
     "machine": true
    }
   },
